course: dictionary
lesson: 6136
title: Mild: not strong, not cold, not harsh
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Mild is a useful word because it can describe many different things, but it always means gentle or not too much. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The winter was mild» tells you the weather was not too cold. «He is a mild man» tells you about his nature: he is calm and gentle.
explain: Food is a good place to test the meaning. On a menu, «mild» is set against «hot», so mild curry means it is not spicy. «Mild cheese» means it does not have a strong taste. Ask yourself: what is the opposite of mild in this sentence? That often tells you the meaning.
explain: In health, mild describes how serious something is. «A mild cold» or «mild symptoms» are not severe. Swap in «not serious» and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: Mild is an adjective, and its comparative forms are milder and mildest.
fact: «Mild» can mean not strong, severe or extreme, as in «a mild illness».
fact: «Mild» can describe weather that is not too cold, as in «a mild winter».
fact: «Mild» can describe food that is not spicy, as in «mild cheese».
fact: «Mild» can describe a person who is gentle and calm, as in «a mild man».
exercise: «The winter was mild, so the flowers bloomed early.» What does mild mean here? | Loud and noisy | *Not too cold | Very icy and dark | Spicy and hot
exercise: On a menu you see «a mild curry» and «a hot curry». Which curry is not spicy? | The extra-hot curry | *The mild curry | The hot curry
exercise: «The mild man smiled and spoke softly.» What kind of man is he? | *Gentle and calm | Tall and strong | Angry and loud
test: «Volunteers carry toads across roads on mild wet nights.» What does mild suggest about the night? | Very dark and stormy | Noisy and busy | *Not too cold | Cold and icy
test: «Poinsettias may cause a mild tummy upset.» Which word is closest in meaning to mild here? | Spicy | Very painful | Deadly | *Not serious
exam: «Eating poinsettias may cause a mild tummy upset, not a serious one.» What does mild mean here? | Spicy and hot | Very strong and painful | Deadly | *Not strong or severe
